 ## Background
-Effective Depth Peeling was introduced by Janghun Kim and Sungkil Lee in 2023 in the paper "Potentially Visible Hidden-Volume Rendering for Multi-View Warping" [S1]. It builds on the concept of Potentially Visible Hidden-Volumes (PVHVs) and extends Depth Peeling by integrating on-the-fly fragment culling. The method is designed to improve efficiency in multi-fragment rendering and remote rendering scenarios [S1].
+Effective Depth Peeling was introduced by Janghun Kim and Sungkil Lee in 2023 in the paper "Potentially Visible Hidden-Volume Rendering for Multi-View Warping" [S1]. It builds on the concept of Potentially Visible Hidden-Volumes (PVHVs) and extends Depth Peeling by integrating on-the-fly fragment culling [S1]. The method is designed to improve efficiency in multi-fragment rendering and remote rendering scenarios [S1].
 
